{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>By what shall I know that I shall inherit it?</b> By what merit. He answered him: by the merit of the sacrifices — this is what He said, ״Take for Me.״ And these names: אל״ף דל״ת, יו״ד ה״א after it, and the intention is: Adonai, in whom is mercy. For Abraham did not prophesy with the attribute of mercy as did Moses, but with אל״ף דל״ת, which is El Shaddai. And the reason that יו״ד ה״א after it is pointed with the vowels of Elohim — you already know that the written Name, one is not permitted to utter it except by the substitute אל״ף דל״ת or by the substitute Elohim: when it stands alone we pronounce it by the substitute אל״ף דל״ת, and the sign for this is (Habakkuk 2:20) ״וה׳ בהיכל קדשו הס מפניו כל הארץ״ — that one should not mention it except in His temple; and when it appears together with אל״ף דל״ת we pronounce it by the substitute Elohim, and the intention in this is toward mercy."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:29.646345874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}